EMAV uses the X window system to provide a graphical user interface under
Linux and an ALSA driver is assumed to be available for the soundcard
to be used with EMAV. The Linux version of EMAV has been tested with
Mandriva Linux 2008 and the Indigo IO soundcard.

The Linux version of EMAV is online at http://audres.org/emav-linux.zip.

EMAV installation:

The executable program file "emav" should be placed in /usr/local/bin.
The  configuration file "emav.ini" should be edited to have the desired
default parameter values and placed in a subdirectory created for EMAV
data files. 

